WEBVTT

1
00:00:11.534 --> 00:00:18.415
"Ahh!" Katie and Joy screamed when the light went out.

2
00:00:18.416 --> 00:00:21.181
"Where's the flashlight?" asked Mom.

3
00:00:21.182 --> 00:00:23.473
But nobody heard her.

4
00:00:23.474 --> 00:00:28.009
The wind sounded like a train roaring over the house.

5
00:00:28.010 --> 00:00:31.380
They could hear it ripping through the trees.

6
00:00:31.381 --> 00:00:37.336
"Heads down," shouted Grandpa as the cellar door rattled.

7
00:00:37.337 --> 00:00:40.383
"Poor Jellybean!" cried Joy.

8
00:00:40.384 --> 00:00:43.624
"It must be so scary out there."

9
00:00:43.625 --> 00:00:46.827
"Magoo is scared too," said Katie.

10
00:00:46.828 --> 00:00:50.301
She could feel the dog shaking in her arms.

11
00:00:50.302 --> 00:00:55.510
And then—whoosh!—the terrible sounds were gone.

12
00:00:55.511 --> 00:00:58.821
Outside, there was silence.

13
00:00:58.822 --> 00:01:02.858
Inside, everybody started to talk at once.

14
00:01:02.859 --> 00:01:05.927
"Anybody hurt?" asked Grandpa.

15
00:01:05.928 --> 00:01:09.016
"That was some wind," said Dad.

16
00:01:09.017 --> 00:01:12.609
"What a tornado!" exclaimed Katie.

17
00:01:12.610 --> 00:01:15.190
"Is it over?" asked Joy.

18
00:01:15.191 --> 00:01:18.384
"We have to find Jellybean!"

19
00:01:18.385 --> 00:01:22.278
"Where's the flashlight?" Mom asked again.

20
00:01:22.279 --> 00:01:25.999
Katie found the flashlight in her box and switched it on.

21
00:01:26.000 --> 00:01:28.683
The beam lit up her face.

22
00:01:28.684 --> 00:01:34.244
She swung the light and saw Mom, Dad, Grandpa, and Joy.

23
00:01:34.245 --> 00:01:38.553
"We're all okay, Captain," said Joy.

24
00:01:38.554 --> 00:01:43.168
The radio crackled, and Mom picked it up to fix the sound.

25
00:01:43.169 --> 00:01:45.850
"Listen," she said.

26
00:01:45.851 --> 00:01:50.724
"The severe weather in Boone County has passed," the announcer said.

27
00:01:50.725 --> 00:01:55.690
"We repeat. The National Weather Service has put out an ALL CLEAR.

28
00:01:55.691 --> 00:01:59.685
The tornado warning for Boone County has ended."

29
00:01:59.686 --> 00:02:03.230
"Look," said Joy. "Sunshine."

30
00:02:03.231 --> 00:02:07.065
Light glowed around the edges of the cellar door.

31
00:02:07.066 --> 00:02:11.460
Magoo slipped out of Katie's arms and ran up the steps.

32
00:02:11.461 --> 00:02:15.157
"Well, let's go see what happened," said Dad.

33
00:02:15.158 --> 00:02:18.689
He climbed the steps and pushed the door open.

34
00:02:18.690 --> 00:02:22.166
"Come on, girls," said Mom.

35
00:02:22.167 --> 00:02:28.616
Outside, Katie and Joy saw a broken flowerpot and a twisted lawn chair.

36
00:02:28.617 --> 00:02:31.914
A section of the garden fence was missing.

37
00:02:31.915 --> 00:02:36.205
Everywhere they looked, tree branches were on the ground.

38
00:02:36.206 --> 00:02:40.598
"The house didn't blow away!" said Katie.

39
00:02:40.599 --> 00:02:43.223
"That's good news," said Dad.

40
00:02:43.224 --> 00:02:46.327
"But there's a broken window in the spare room."

41
00:02:46.328 --> 00:02:49.582
Grandpa picked something up from the ground.

42
00:02:49.583 --> 00:02:53.316
"Here's one of my garden gloves," he said.

43
00:02:53.317 --> 00:02:57.189
"Let's go check the garden," said Mom.

44
00:02:57.190 --> 00:03:00.374
"And the chickens," said Joy.

45
00:03:00.375 --> 00:03:02.978
Katie and Joy ran ahead.

46
00:03:02.979 --> 00:03:07.173
"The lettuce is smashed!" called Katie.

47
00:03:07.174 --> 00:03:12.697
"The peas are in the mud!" called Joy as she ran along the fence.

48
00:03:12.698 --> 00:03:15.969
"Forget about the green beans!"

49
00:03:15.970 --> 00:03:21.082
Grandpa, Mom, and Dad caught up with the twins and looked at the garden.

50
00:03:21.083 --> 00:03:27.366
"I'm pretty sure my watermelon seeds got washed away," said Joy with a sigh.

51
00:03:27.367 --> 00:03:30.684
"We can get more seeds," said Grandpa.

52
00:03:30.685 --> 00:03:33.561
"There's nothing here we can't fix."

53
00:03:33.562 --> 00:03:36.225
"I hear the chickens!" said Joy.

54
00:03:36.226 --> 00:03:40.594
"I'm coming!" she called as she ran to the coop.

55
00:03:40.595 --> 00:03:45.884
When she opened the door, the chickens hurried out, fussing and clucking.

56
00:03:45.885 --> 00:03:48.442
Joy looked around.

57
00:03:48.443 --> 00:03:51.353
"Everything looks okay here," she called.

58
00:03:51.354 --> 00:03:53.674
"Let's check the tree house!"

59
00:03:53.675 --> 00:03:57.470
She turned toward the pond and ran a few steps.

60
00:03:57.471 --> 00:04:01.797
"Oh no!" she cried, looking up the hill.

61
00:04:01.798 --> 00:04:04.317
She ran a few steps more.

62
00:04:04.318 --> 00:04:07.586
"Part of the tree house got crushed!"

63
00:04:07.587 --> 00:04:12.802
She suddenly remembered that Jellybean was still missing and gasped.

64
00:04:12.803 --> 00:04:16.430
"Poor cat," she murmured.

65
00:04:16.431 --> 00:04:18.910
"Let's go see," said Dad.

66
00:04:18.911 --> 00:04:23.005
He and Joy hurried to the tree house and climbed the steps.

67
00:04:23.006 --> 00:04:26.842
Dad cleared branches from the window and looked around.

68
00:04:26.843 --> 00:04:29.690
"I see some broken boards," he said.

69
00:04:29.691 --> 00:04:31.975
"But we can repair everything.

70
00:04:31.976 --> 00:04:37.239
All we need is a good set of tools and teamwork. Right, partner?"

71
00:04:37.240 --> 00:04:39.970
"Right!" Joy said.

72
00:04:39.971 --> 00:04:42.132
Then her eyes opened wide.

73
00:04:42.133 --> 00:04:44.404
"Did you hear that?"

74
00:04:44.405 --> 00:04:46.858
"What?" said Dad.

75
00:04:46.859 --> 00:04:49.956
"Listen," said Joy.

76
00:04:49.957 --> 00:04:53.230
MEEEOOOW!

77
00:04:53.231 --> 00:04:56.944
"Jellybean's alive!" cried Joy.

78
00:04:56.945 --> 00:05:02.570
Dad got down on his knees and looked under a pile of branches and wood.

79
00:05:02.571 --> 00:05:07.279
He reached in and pulled out a wet gray cat.

80
00:05:07.280 --> 00:05:13.211
Joy scooped up the shivering Jellybean in her arms and leaned out the window.

81
00:05:13.212 --> 00:05:17.020
"All the Donovans are okay!" she said.

82
00:05:17.021 --> 00:05:25.665
"Five people, six chickens, one dog—and one great cat!"
